steps.message:
The 2.2 binaries have only 2026 (404) captures — the original files were never archived under these paths. Let me do a broad domain-wide CDX search for any 2.2 source capture, and test SourceForge with full browser headers plus the classic funet.fi mirror.

{
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo '=== BROAD CDX: povray.org domain, 2.2, 200 ==='; curl -sSL -A 'Mozilla/5.0' 'http://web.archive.org/cdx/search/cdx?url=povray.org&matchType=domain&output=text&fl=timestamp,original,statuscode,length&filter=statuscode:200&filter=original:.*2\\.2.*&collapse=urlkey&limit=400' 2>&1 | awk '$4+0>3000' | head -50\n",
      "duration": 40.0
    }
  ]
}

The Wayback snapshot serving works for real binaries (the .exe came back intact at 621KB). So archive.org can serve actual files — I just need to find a large (real) capture of the 2.2 source. Let me search the whole domain for large captures that match source-file names.

{
  "analysis": "Confirmed: Wayback snapshot serving works for real binaries (a 621KB .exe downloaded intact). The 'temporarily offline' was transient. Live povray.org is still CF-blocked. Now I need to find a LARGE (real) capture of the 2.2 source on archive.org, not the small HTML interstitial pages.",
  "plan": "Search the whole povray.org domain in CDX for captures with length >100000 bytes (real binaries) that match 2.2/src/source/tar/tgz names. This should surface the actual source tarball capture.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "echo '=== large captures on povray.org matching source/2.2 ==='; curl -sSL -A 'Mozilla/5.0' 'http://web.archive.org/cdx/search/cdx?url=povray.org&matchType=domain&output=text&fl=timestamp,original,statuscode,length&filter=length:>100000&collapse=urlkey&limit=4000' 2>&1 | grep -iE '2\\.2|src|source|tar|tgz|unix|\.Z' | awk '{print $1, $4, $2}' | sort -k2 -n | tail -50\n",
      "duration": 50.0
    }
  ]
}
